editorial:
## Method and reasoning
Track each unresolved height and the earliest index where it can start. A shorter bar closes all taller stack entries at the previous index. Carry the popped start to the new height so it can extend left. Keep equal heights in one entry using the earliest start. A zero-height sentinel flushes the stack. Width times height needs long long.

## Walk through the sample
When the height drops from 6 to 2, first close height 6 at width 1, then height 5 at width 2. The second rectangle contributes 10. Its width includes the taller bar because both support height 5.

## Complexity
Time and space are O(n).

## Reference implementation
~~~
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    int n;
    cin >> n;
    vector<pair<long long, int>> stack;
    long long best = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {
        long long h = 0;
        if (i < n)
            cin >> h;
        int start = i;
        while (!stack.empty() && stack.back().first > h) {
            auto [height, left] = stack.back();
            stack.pop_back();
            best = max(best, height * (i - left));
            start = left;
        }
        if (stack.empty() || stack.back().first < h)
            stack.emplace_back(h, start);
    }
    cout << best << '\n';
}
~~~
